## [ENT-001] | 2026-07-20 07:35 UTC | Link | error | ref: reflections/2026-07-20_link_first-session-onboarding.md
Session-end corrections from Suggi review: (1) IOR had version history
table on v1 file -- removed per template-reflections.md rule. (2) Memory
file headers were inconsistent between birth and session-end entries --
restructured to standard format (## YYYY-MM-DD (HH:MM UTC) -- <title>).
(3) IOR timestamp was future + rounded (07:45:00Z) -- fixed to real UTC
(07:32:14Z). Gate added: AGENTS.md session-end item 2 now explicitly
states "Do NOT add version history table on v1 files." Protocol.md now
requires reading before writing logbook entries.

## [ENT-002] | 2026-08-01 21:32 UTC | Link | error | ref: reflections/2026-08-01_link_default-preset-cannot-remove-open-tiles.md
Skill-load gap: exact-match skill (hermes-desktop-troubleshooting) not loaded at session start for a desktop-misbehaves task.
Root cause: partial skill scanning - loaded a related CDP skill instead of the trigger-exact playbook.
Fix: load the most specific matching skill first; the skill layer already covers the class (R8, no duplication added).

## [ENT-003] | 2026-08-05 12:35 UTC | Ava | error | ref: reflections/2026-08-05_ava_status-flags-are-snapshots-not-verdicts.md
Run-status misreports: reported writer "never dispatched" and discoverer
"errored" from run-log snapshots; both were in-flight or auto-retried.
Root cause: treating visible state as complete state; run logs only show
completions. Fix: verify running_at_ms, retry history, retryOn config
before declaring failure. Also: unauthorized library.log ENT-056 write
(wrong number, line-count derivation). Fix: logbook writes only at
session-end or on instruction; ENT read from file tail.

## [ENT-004] | 2026-08-31 11:19 UTC | Morpheus | error | ref: reflections/2026-08-31_morpheus_stateful-runtime-upgrade-is-a-data-migration.md
OpenClaw staged-newer-CLI dry-run advanced the live old-state schema before
the subcommand preview, making the old CLI unable to reopen shared state.
Root cause: subcommand dry-run semantics were assumed to cover process-startup
migrations. Fix: preview only through the installed CLI or isolated state;
the personal OpenClaw upgrade gate now enforces this boundary.

## [ENT-005] | 2026-08-31 11:19 UTC | Morpheus | error | ref: reflections/2026-08-31_morpheus_stateful-runtime-upgrade-is-a-data-migration.md
OpenClaw Doctor failed with `EACCES` under `sudo -u openclaw` although Ava's
state ownership was correct. Strace found child processes inheriting
Morpheus's private workspace cwd.
Root cause: changing user identity did not change cwd. Fix: every cross-user
OpenClaw command runs from `/tmp` or another runtime-user-readable directory.

## [ENT-006] | 2026-08-31 11:19 UTC | Morpheus | error | ref: reflections/2026-08-31_morpheus_stateful-runtime-upgrade-is-a-data-migration.md
OpenClaw 2.0 was reported complete after local HTTP, RPC, plugin, memory, and
route-map checks, but Suggi's exact Tailscale browser URL returned HTTP 403
`proxy_attribution_required`.
Root cause: the completion gate proved components, not the user's ingress
path. Fix: the upgrade gate now requires the exact URL to return HTTP 200 and
records narrow loopback proxy trust with token auth retained.
